<h1>DocsFixture</h1>
<p class="where">interface, schema fstar-module-docs version 2</p>
<div class="decl"><div><span class="name">DocsFixture.incr</span><span class="kind">val</span></div><div class="sig">x: Prims.int -&gt; Prims.int</div><div class="where">DocsFixture.fsti(23,0-23,22)</div><div class="doc">Increments &#x27;x&#x27;.

This text is written in the interface, which is what clients of
this module see. Opaque text is escaped by the HTML renderer:
&lt;unsafe&gt; &amp; &quot;quoted&quot;.</div></div>
<div class="decl"><div><span class="name">DocsFixture.colour</span><span class="kind">type</span></div><div class="sig">Type0</div><div class="where">DocsFixture.fsti(34,5-34,11)</div><div class="doc">A tiny colour.
The typechecker copies the attributes of a type definition onto each
of its data constructors, so this text must be reported for &#x27;colour&#x27;
and for neither &#x27;Red&#x27; nor &#x27;Blue&#x27;.</div></div>
